# presenter.env.example — copy to presenter.env.local and fill in.
#
#   cp presenter.env.example presenter.env.local
#   chmod 600 presenter.env.local
#
# presenter.env.local is gitignored and MUST NOT be committed. The presenter CLI
# loads it WITHOUT ever echoing MODEL_API_KEY; the key is only ever reported as
# set/unset — never the value, a length, or any partial characters.
#
# The demo drives a real OpenAI model. Baseline kagent uses the key directly;
# protect replaces it with a dummy and mounts the real key only into Aksh for
# policy-gated injection. A real key spends real quota, so:
#   * use a free-tier / low-cost key,
#   * `demo.sh doctor` and `demo.sh setup` make NO model calls,
#   * `demo.sh validate --model` makes exactly one readiness call,
#   * `demo.sh validate --full`/`--mac` make a small bounded number of calls.

# REQUIRED — your OpenAI API key (starts with sk-...). SECRET — never printed,
# never rendered into a Kubernetes Secret YAML or command argument.
MODEL_API_KEY=

# REQUIRED — the OpenAI model to use.
MODEL_NAME=gpt-5.4-mini

# The endpoint is intentionally fixed by the CLI to
# https://api.openai.com/v1 so it cannot drift from the protected policy.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Entra credential-theft scenario (optional but recommended).
#
# The headline demo shows a prompt-injected agent leaking its mounted CLOUD
# CREDENTIAL, and Aksh stopping it. When the Azure CLI is logged in, `setup`
# mints a REAL Microsoft Entra access token (via `az account get-access-token`)
# and mounts it as that credential — so a baseline leak is undeniably a real
# Entra token (the collector decodes it to prove issuer/audience/tenant). The
# token authenticates nothing sensitive here and expires in ~1h.
#
#   az login                       # once, before the demo
#
# If `az` is not logged in, `setup` falls back to a clearly-synthetic demo
# credential and the scenario still runs (just without the "it's a real Entra
# token" reveal). Override the Azure resource whose token is used if needed:
# AZURE_CRED_RESOURCE=https://cognitiveservices.azure.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional overrides (defaults shown; uncomment to change). These let the CLI
# adapt as the sibling workstreams (collector/MCP, injector, kagent manifests)
# settle on names. Leave commented to use the built-in contract defaults.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLUSTER=agentcon-japan
# DEMO_NS=agentcon-demo
# TELEMETRY_HOST=telemetry.ops-insights.example
# COLLECTOR_NS=ops-insights
# COLLECTOR_SVC=telemetry
# COLLECTOR_PORT=80
# COLLECTOR_LOCAL_PORT=18080
# KAGENT_UI_LOCAL_PORT=18081
# PROXY_IMAGE=aksh-proxy:agentcon
# INJECTOR_IMAGE=aksh-injector:agentcon
# INJECT_LABEL_KEY=aksh.dev/inject
# INJECT_LABEL_VALUE=enabled
